Value Required LOCAL_INTERFACE (\S+)
Value CHASSIS_ID (\S+)
Value NEIGHBOR_PORT_ID (.*)
Value NEIGHBOR_NAME (.*)
Value NEIGHBOR_DESCRIPTION (.*)
Value MGMT_ADDRESS (.*)
Value CAPABILITIES (.*)

# Built from a real `show lldp neighbor-info detail` capture off an
# ArubaOS-CX 6300-series switch.
#
# Confirmed live (2026-08-26) against a real ArubaOS-CX 6300 stack
# (16 LLDP neighbors) that a neighbor's Mac-Phy/EEE block --
# "Neighbor Mac-Phy details", "Neighbor Auto-neg Supported",
# "Neighbor MAU type", "Neighbor EEE information", per-direction wake
# and echo times, etc. -- was falling through every specific rule
# straight into the trailing catch-all, which aborted the ENTIRE parse
# on the first neighbor record and silently returned zero neighbors for
# a switch that had sixteen. The generic `^Neighbor\s` rule below soaks
# up that whole block (and any other "Neighbor <field>" line this vendor
# adds in a future firmware) without enumerating every sub-field by
# name; it sits after every rule that captures a Value so those still
# win first.
#
# A second, unrelated gap hit the same way (confirmed live 2026-08-26
# against a real capture with 17 neighbors): a Comware neighbor's
# System-Description wraps onto multiple lines with NO field-label
# prefix on the continuation lines at all --
#   Neighbor System-Description    : HP Comware Platform Software, ...
#   HP 5500-48G-PoE+-4SFP HI Switch with 2 Interface Slots
#   Copyright (c) 2010-2018 Hewlett Packard Enterprise Development LP
#   Neighbor Chassis-ID            : ...
# -- so no fixed pattern can be added for it; it is unpredictable free
# text from whatever the far-end device happens to advertise. Because
# this platform is BestEffort (see internal/crawler/plan.go) and this
# command's real-world output has now proven messy in two independent
# ways neither anticipated up front, the trailing catch-all was changed
# from erroring out (aborting the whole capture) to matching and
# silently dropping the line instead: an unrecognized line loses at
# most the extra field it was on, never the rest of the device's
# neighbors. LOCAL_INTERFACE stays Required, so a record still cannot
# be emitted without a real "Port :" line establishing it.
#
# Record boundary is the next "Port :" line rather than the trailing dash
# separator, because the LAST block in a real capture has no trailing
# separator before the stripped prompt. The very last record in the file
# therefore still depends on gotextfsm's implicit EOF-Record when no
# explicit EOF state is defined — standard TextFSM behavior, but the one
# assumption in this file that most wants confirming.
Start
  ^Port\s*:\s*\S+\s*$$ -> Continue.Record
  ^Port\s*:\s*${LOCAL_INTERFACE}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+Entries\s
  ^Neighbor\s+System-Name\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_NAME}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+System-Description\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_DESCRIPTION}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+Chassis-ID\s*:\s*${CHASSIS_ID}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+Management-Address\s*:\s*${MGMT_ADDRESS}\s*$$
  ^Chassis\s+Capabilities\s+Available
  ^Chassis\s+Capabilities\s+Enabled\s*:\s*${CAPABILITIES}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+Port-ID\s*:\s*${NEIGHBOR_PORT_ID}\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s+Port-Desc
  ^Neighbor\s+Port\s+VLAN
  ^Neighbor\s+Port\s+MFS
  ^Link\s+aggregation
  ^Aggregation\s+port\s+ID
  ^TTL\s*:
  ^-+\s*$$
  ^LLDP\s+Neighbor\s+Information\s*$$
  ^=+\s*$$
  ^Total\s+Neighbor\s+Entries
  ^\s*$$
  ^Neighbor\s
  ^.*
